would be at the White House for a UFC fight on June 14, his 80th birthday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UFC eyes Africa for its next big event</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e49092cac844d97f2c842d6ee7bb0e1d721327e18b94e3b5a0964805302c711</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:43Z</updated><published>2024-08-18T12:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ufc-eyes-africa-for-its-next-big-event/a-69971786--a57df6539cce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ufc-eyes-africa-for-its-next-big-event/a-69971786?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A high-profile win by South African Dricus du Plessis over Nigerian-born Israel Adesanya has paved the way for a potential UFC event in Africa. The mixed martial arts format has yet to host a bout on the continent.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Women's football in Germany booming, but still much to do</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d2202928b8e2b1643db54555bc09c31b9e218f826467d01bd20df918d7a65e88</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T04:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687--313365dcb46e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-football-in-germany-booming-but-still-much-to-do/a-79291687?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Women's football is growing rapidly, particularly in Germany. Nevertheless, equal pay and investment remain major talking points.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>VAR's mission creep a problem for football</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c5cbd0ce7cd2017d5b455f6099b97014c7658c6284f74683ce14255e955fb30</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642--644b469bed29.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/var-s-mission-creep-a-problem-for-football/a-79272642?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a decade of use, questions around VAR in football are louder than ever. Has the technology strayed too far from its remit?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Ovechkin backs Putin party in campaign video</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4af5867e016c652ec522fc850a60f9374eac5174463573954c932ca19e349e1b</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772--a8049deceb76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-ovechkin-backs-putin-party-in-campaign-video/a-79277772?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ice hockey legend Alexander Ovechkin has lent Vladimir Putin's party a helping hand in its parliamentary election campaign. That's in keeping with a pattern of support by an athlete who claims not to be political.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>After Neuer: Who will be Germany's new No. 1 goalkeeper?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ce415e00693ef86d0fdbbcbc5ae28a0833ee1b6d7d24f3f1d1f01a1c0f5c93d3</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T14:25:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377--1d35484fc587.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-neuer-who-will-be-germany-s-new-no-1-goalkeeper/a-79276377?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Following Manuel Neuer's retirement, there are many candidates to succeed him, but which goalkeeper will Jürgen Klopp choose? What factors will play a role? And will Neuer's future have an indirect influence?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Women's Basketball World Cup: Can Germany harness a boom?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:594c7e668cc578b49ffdb47d88eeeb4441bddddcf4fe70eba4586b36ff0d5bc1</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-14T15:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602--77d972e02866.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/women-s-basketball-world-cup-can-germany-harness-a-boom/a-79263602?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany thrilled fans at the Women's Basketball World Cup. But even if this sparked a boom in the women's game, the infrastructure simply isn't ready for it.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>EU sports commissioner says FIFA is 'damaging to football'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e90b6d59a2e3c675848910ff0c873dfdda580ca17391be813bbe36a0d601bb91</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T07:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424--c7a4bd30a298.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-sports-commissioner-says-fifa-is-damaging-to-football/a-79193424?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Speaking to DW, EU Commissioner Glenn Micallef hit out at world football's governing body over its "poor governance."</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Afghanistan's women: A national soccer team without a home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74df50533b287be4dad607760acae0df2802108062a69ba0e7135025ef17eb01</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500--7cfb666b9c3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Afghan women's national football team has finally been officially recognized by FIFA. Now the players want to make history both on and off the field.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Egg freezing in women's football: Choice or pressure?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8771eb3f942cdfdb8c736d245914e9087ab2a43c60b33f2ee6e5dd31f3642445</id><updated>2026-09-23T04:54:43Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/egg-freezing-in-women-s-football-choice-or-pressure/a-79145259--8a56ba698069.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/egg-freezing-in-women-s-football-choice-or-pressure/a-79145259?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's football federation is set to join a handful of clubs in paying for female players to freeze their eggs. Experts have welfare concerns.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
